      "group-2024-jslk-reading-a": {
        "groupId": "group-2024-jslk-reading-a",
        "groupType": "reading",
        "title": "Reading A",
        "questionIds": ["q-2024-jslk-021","q-2024-jslk-022","q-2024-jslk-023"],
        "passage": {
          "paragraphs": [
            { "paragraphId": "para-2024-jslk-reading-a-title", "text": "Yellowstone Poster Exhibition to Be on View at UW's Coe Library" },
            { "paragraphId": "para-2024-jslk-reading-a-p1", "text": "A first-of-its-kind exhibition that focuses on the history of Yellowstone National Park posters will be on display at the University of Wyoming's Coe Library from January 26 through Tuesday, May 31." },
            { "paragraphId": "para-2024-jslk-reading-a-p2", "text": "\"Wonderland Illustrated\" will present posters and poster-style illustrations of the park spanning from the 1870s through 2021. The exhibition is a collaboration between the university and the Buffalo Bill Center of the West in Cody, Wyoming, in honor of the 150th anniversary of the park." },
            { "paragraphId": "para-2024-jslk-reading-a-p3", "text": "\"We're thrilled to be working with Yellowstone collectors Jack and Susan Davis, and Larry and Thea Lancaster to bring this unique display of rarely-seen Yellowstone visual materials to campus,\" said head of UW Libraries Special Collections Tamsen Hert." },
            { "paragraphId": "para-2024-jslk-reading-a-p4", "text": "One poster from the exhibition - Henry Wellge's \"Yellowstone National Park\" from 1904 - was recently purchased with donations from multiple sources and is one of only a few known copies worldwide." }
          ]
        }
      },

      "group-2024-jslk-reading-b": {
        "groupId": "group-2024-jslk-reading-b",
        "groupType": "reading",
        "title": "Reading B",
        "questionIds": ["q-2024-jslk-024","q-2024-jslk-025","q-2024-jslk-026","q-2024-jslk-027"],
        "passage": {
          "paragraphs": [
            { "paragraphId": "para-2024-jslk-reading-b-p1", "text": "Parrots are prey animals, which means that other predators in the wild, such as hawks or snakes, are looking to make them into a meal." },
            { "paragraphId": "para-2024-jslk-reading-b-p2", "text": "Parrots are most easily hurt when feeding on the ground; membership in a group plays an important function in ensuring the safety of parrots in the wild." },
            { "paragraphId": "para-2024-jslk-reading-b-p3", "text": "As prey animals, parrots are constantly watching out for danger and they instinctively react to risks. Their first choice is always to take flight." },
            { "paragraphId": "para-2024-jslk-reading-b-p4", "text": "Because their biggest enemy is the hawk, parrots are especially reactive to quick movements from above and behind. For this reason, things like balloons, which move quickly in unpredictable ways, can be very frightening for a parrot." },
            { "paragraphId": "para-2024-jslk-reading-b-p5", "text": "As prey animals, parrots are often frightened by exposure to new household items or strangers. It is important to expose your parrot slowly and carefully to new things." }
          ]
        }
      },

      "group-2024-jslk-reading-c": {
        "groupId": "group-2024-jslk-reading-c",
        "groupType": "reading",
        "title": "Reading C",
        "questionIds": ["q-2024-jslk-028","q-2024-jslk-029","q-2024-jslk-030","q-2024-jslk-031"],
        "passage": {
          "paragraphs": [
            { "paragraphId": "para-2024-jslk-reading-c-p1", "text": "In his 1936 work How to Win Friends and Influence People, Dale Carnegie wrote: \"I have come to the conclusion that there is only one way under high heaven to get the best of an argument - and that is to avoid it.\"" },
            { "paragraphId": "para-2024-jslk-reading-c-p2", "text": "Carnegie would be right if arguments were fights, which is how we often think of them. Like physical fights, verbal fights can leave both sides battered and never settle anything. It can seem that the only way to come out ahead is to avoid them altogether." },
            { "paragraphId": "para-2024-jslk-reading-c-p3", "text": "However, there are ways to win an argument every time. When you state your position, formulate an argument for what you believe and spell out the reasons for why you think you're right." },
            { "paragraphId": "para-2024-jslk-reading-c-p4", "text": "These tools can help you win every argument - not in the unhelpful sense of beating your opponents but in the better sense of learning about the issues that divide people." }
          ]
        }
      },
      "group-2024-jslk-reading-d": {
        "groupId": "group-2024-jslk-reading-d",
        "groupType": "reading",
        "title": "Reading D",
        "questionIds": ["q-2024-jslk-032","q-2024-jslk-033","q-2024-jslk-034","q-2024-jslk-035"],
        "passage": {
          "paragraphs": [
            { "paragraphId": "para-2024-jslk-reading-d-p1", "text": "For lots of kids, toddlerhood is an important time for friendship. Studies show that the earlier kids learn to form positive relationships, the better they will be at relating to people throughout their lives." },
            { "paragraphId": "para-2024-jslk-reading-d-p2", "text": "Even so, how quickly your child develops into a social creature may also depend on his temperament. Some toddlers are naturally outgoing, while others tend to be shy." },
            { "paragraphId": "para-2024-jslk-reading-d-p3", "text": "This seemingly unusual way of demonstrating fondness can result in unpleasant behavior. Regardless of how much they like a playmate, toddlers tend to lack the social skills needed to play cooperatively." },
            { "paragraphId": "para-2024-jslk-reading-d-p4", "text": "Begin by helping your child learn sympathy (\"Ben is crying. What's making him so sad?\"), then suggest how he could resolve the situation." },
            { "paragraphId": "para-2024-jslk-reading-d-p5", "text": "Another way to encourage healthy social interaction is by encouraging kids to use words - not fists - to express how they feel." }
          ]
        }
      },

